/-!
# BuiData2: the exported RD=2 king Bui certificate

The 185-type king convolution system at split window RD = 2 and its exact
rational super-solution at x = 106251/1000000, giving the conditional bound
`lambda <= 1000000/106251` = 9.411676 (see `Upper/BuiRD2.lean`).

Machine-generated by `scripts/gen_bui_cert.lean.py --rd 2` from the system of
`experiments/king_bui.py` / `experiments/king_certificate.py` (canonical 'll'
casing, eps = 1e-3, repair converged after 92 sweeps); cross-checked
against `python3 -m experiments.king_certificate 2` (same x, exact-check PASS).
Do not edit by hand; regenerate instead.

`buiRD2_valid` is the *entire arithmetic side* of the certificate: index
bounds, rank descent, and the cleared-denominator super-solution inequalities,
checked by `decide +kernel`.  The combinatorial side stays a named hypothesis
(`KingBuiSystemRD2Holds`).
-/

